@scene chapter_2_trial_of_choice

background: valley_vista.jpg
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"You step through the doorway, and the endless hall folds shut behind you like a closing book."
"Warm air — real air, with weather in it. A valley opens beneath you, green and river-threaded, mountains standing in the far haze."

npc You:
"So this is what was on the other side of the door."

background: green_valley.jpg

dialogue:
"You walk down through long grass to the dark treeline at the valley's edge."

background: deep_forest.jpg

dialogue:
"The trees close over you. No bird sings, no leaf moves — only your own footsteps, and then—"

npc Unknown:
"AAAGH!"

dialogue:
"You run toward it. Branches whip past. The trees part."

background: forest_gate.png

dialogue:
"An enormous stone gate, carved into the mountainside, its runes pulsing."
"At its base lies an old man in a tattered cloak, barely conscious."

background: elder_mage.png

npc You:
"Sir! Are you alright?"

dialogue:
"He opens his eyes. A faint smile."

npc Old Man:
"Traveller... please. Decades I have spent on this gate, and age has caught up with me."
"Open it, and I will pay you in something better than treasure."

dialogue:
"He looks directly into your eyes."

npc Old Man:
"Knowledge."
"And after — a name. Halvard, who keeps the scales two valleys east."
"He weighs, and compares, and calls one thing greater than another. That is a magic of its own, and you will need it before the road is done."

background: forest_gate.png

dialogue:
"The runes flare. The ground trembles."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"TRIAL OF CHOICE"
"Teach the gate how to decide."

dialogue:
"The old man rises on his staff and lays a hand on the stone. Three symbols ignite and hang waiting."
"🔥 Fire · 🌊 Water · 🌿 Nature"

npc Old Man:
"The Gate of Choices. Strength cannot open it — it obeys only the law of decisions."
"You already carry the spells you need, {{player_name}}: input() to ask, print() to declare."
"What you lack is the power to CHOOSE between them."

dialogue:
"He taps the gate twice with his staff. The runes rearrange into a glowing command."
"[Enter a number between 1, 2 and 3.]"

npc Old Man:
"One opens Fire. Two, Water. Three, Nature. Any other number, and the gate must refuse."
"It cannot think for itself. It follows only the instructions it is given."
"But not all at once. A choice between THREE begins as a choice between two."

dialogue:
"A single rune detaches from the arch and hovers at eye level, pulsing with a reading of raw power."

system system:
"MISSION"
"One test, two outcomes. If the reading passes the threshold, name it. Otherwise, call it normal."

mission: control_flow_intro

npc Old Man:
"Good. IF the condition holds, one road. ELSE, the other. There is no third door yet."
"Now — the gate asks for three."

dialogue:
"The runes begin assembling into lines of unfinished code."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Write an if / elif / else statement."
"1 → Fire · 2 → Water · 3 → Nature"
"Anything else → 'Enter number between 1, 2 and 3.'"

dialogue:
"The old man steps back. The gate waits in silence."

mission: trial_of_choice

background: forest_gate.png

dialogue:
"Your code settles into the runes and holds."
"All three symbols blaze at once — Fire, Water, Nature, each obeying the choice you taught it."
"The great stone doors shudder, and begin to part."

npc Old Man:
"After all these years. You taught it in a single sitting what I could not grasp in a lifetime."

dialogue:
"He presses a worn token into your hand, etched with a single open eye."

npc Old Man:
"Knowledge, as I promised. The road ahead is long, and the Blight has walked it before you."
"Bridges that will not hold. Caravans that have lost their order. Books that have forgotten their own names."
"But you asked the gate a question today — 'is this one, or two, or three' — and it answered."

dialogue:
"He taps the token in your palm."

npc Old Man:
"Every question of that kind rests on something underneath: knowing which of two things is GREATER. Which is EQUAL. Which is neither."
"Halvard has spent forty years on that one problem, and he will hand it to you in an afternoon."
"Go east to the scales. Learn to weigh before you learn to endure."

dialogue:
"Beyond the open gate, a path winds east, toward a thin column of chimney smoke."
"You step through."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"Trial of Choice"
"Mastered: if · elif · else"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 50
achievement: MASTER OF CHOICES

next:
chapter_2b_alchemists_scales
